            <ArticleTitle>Chlorhexidine-Induced Chemical Burns in Very Low Birth Weight Infants.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>262-265.e2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0022-3476(17)31056-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jpeds.2017.08.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Skin disinfection with chlorhexidine gluconate has not been standardized in preterm infants. We present 5 cases of chemical burns that occurred within the first 2 days of life in very low birth weight neonates after skin disinfection with aqueous and alcohol-based chlorhexidine solutions.</AbstractText>
